 "title": "Register of Deeds - Oglala Lakota County, South Dakota",
 "text": "Register of Deeds - Oglala Lakota County, South Dakota\nSkip to content\nOctober 18, 2026\nOglala Lakota County, South Dakota\nHome\nOnline Map\nAbout\nDirectory »\nAuditors & Welfare Office\nClerk of Court\nPublic Health Nurse\nDirector of Equalization\nEmergency Management\nGIS\nHighway Department\nPlanning & Zoning\nRegister of Deeds\nSheriff\nState’s Attorney\nTreasurer\nVeterans Service Officer\nWeed & Pest\nCommission »\nCounty Commissioners\n2026 Minute Archive\n2025 Minute Archive\n2024 Minute Archive\nOlder Minute Archive\nEmployment (2)\nQuick Links\nFall River Co.\nRegister of Deeds\nNOTICE REGARDING COUNTY NAME CHANGE\nServices\nSouth Dakota Vital Records (Please note that all certified copies are $15.00 each):\nApplication form (required) & additional form for multiple birth records:\nBirth, Marriage, or Death record [form]\nMultiple Birth Records [form]\nSpecial Fee Waivers for Vital Records (please read Fee Waiver Requirements):\nFee Waiver Request (Birth Record) [form]\nMilitary Fee Waiver Request (Birth, Marriage or Death record) [form]\nMarriage License Information: Must be applied for in person at Register of Deeds office within South Dakota. The license is usable immediately, however only valid for 20 days following issuance. Please note that you will need to know the location of where the ceremony will take place prior to requesting the license and will also need to secure a qualified individual to solemnize the marriage.\nMarriage License Application [form]\nMarriage Parental Consent Form (between the ages of 16 & 18)\nFurther information pertaining to marriage licenses\nNot finding what you need? Please use the link: Vital Records South Dakota Department of Health .\nReal Estate Document Recording & Filing of Federal, State, County, and Mechanic’s Liens:\nInformation on recording Real Estate Documents in South Dakota County Procedure for E-Recording Recording Fees\nTransfer Fee Exemption Statute\nPassport Information Passport Acceptance Facility\nMilitary Discharges Filing of Military Discharges Authorization for Release of Certfiicate of Military Discharge [form]\nFictitious Business Name Filing of Fictitious of Business Names\nRecords\nThere are no searchable records online. Please contact the Register of Deeds by phone or email with any information requests.\nMission\nThe county Register of Deeds issues and/or files marriage licenses, birth and death certificates, burial permits, real estate transactions (including deeds, mortgages and mortgage transfers), federal and state tax liens, state unemployment tax liens, military discharge records, and business name registrations. The Register of Deeds is also responsible for recording all liens, survey plat certificates and county welfare liens. The Register of Deeds is the official county record keeper.\nRegister of Deeds: Melody Engebretson\nDeputy Register of Deeds: Amber Tschacher\n906 N. River St.\nHot Springs, SD 57747\nPhone: (605) 745-5139\nFax: (605) 745-3708\nrod@oglalalakotacountysd.gov\nQuick Links\nAuditors & Welfare Office\nAbsentee Voting\nElections\nVoter Registration\nVoter Identification\nSD State Election Resources\nSD State Voter Portal\n2026 Summer Reassessment\nNational Active Fires Map\nWebsite Survey\nWebsite Survey\nPlease let us know about your visit to our site.\nWhere did you hear about this website? * Search Engine Friend Other\nWhat were your reasons for looking at our site? *\nGeneral Information\nSpecific Information\nCuriosity\nOther\nDid you find what you were looking for? *\nYes\nNo\nMaybe\nIf no, what information were you looking for? (Please be specific so that we can improve our website.) *\nIf you would like a response to your request for additional information please list your email below.\nSubmit\nReturn to top of page\nCopyright © 2026 on Genesis Framework · WordPress · Log in\nNotifications",
